Privacy Policy for Wakanda Browser
​Effective Date: October 1, 2026
Last Updated: October 1, 2026
​At Wakanda Browser ("we," "our," or "us"), your privacy is our top priority. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our mobile application and related web services.
​1. Information We Collect
​We only collect data necessary to provide and improve Wakanda Browser’s core features:
​AI & Content Data: When you use AI Features (e.g., Summarize Page, Webpage Q&A, or Task Detection), webpage text and content are processed temporarily to generate accurate summaries, identify deadlines, or extract tasks.
​Voice Data: Voice commands are processed strictly when you tap the voice button to trigger voice search or navigation. Voice data is used exclusively to fulfill your voice requests.
​Usage & Device Information: Anonymous technical data such as app crash reports, OS version, performance metrics, and device model to ensure stability and smooth performance.
​Security & Threat Data: Web URLs visited are screened against real-time phishing and scam databases to protect you from fraudulent websites.
​2. How We Use Your Information
​We use the collected information solely for the following purposes:
​To Deliver Core AI Features: Summarizing web content, creating tasks, detecting deadlines, and displaying reminders.
​To Enable Hands-Free Navigation: Executing voice commands, smart auto-scrolling, and read-aloud functionality.
​To Enhance Web Security: Identifying and blocking phishing attempts, scam sites, and malicious links.
​To Sync Local Features: Storing your Read Later articles, local calendar events, and task list on your device.
​3. Disclosure of AI-Generated Content
​Wakanda Browser utilizes Artificial Intelligence (AI) to generate webpage summaries, task suggestions, and automated voice navigation. AI-generated outputs are created dynamically to assist your browsing experience and are presented clearly within the app interface.
​4. Data Sharing and Third-Party Services
​We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data to third parties.
​AI & Cloud Service Providers: Limited webpage text data may be securely processed through trusted third-party cloud APIs strictly to power AI features (e.g., text summarization and voice processing).
​Security Services: Threat queries are hashed or processed anonymously to check against security protection engines.
​Legal Compliance: We may disclose information only if required by law, regulation, or legal process.
​5. Storage and Data Retention
​Local Storage: Your bookmarks, tasks, reminders, and "Read Later" lists are stored locally on your device unless synced with your linked calendar or task services.
​Transient AI Processing: Text submitted for AI processing is discarded immediately after generating summaries or processing voice actions and is not permanently retained.
​6. Your Rights and Data Control
​You maintain full control over your data within Wakanda Browser:
​Permissions Management: You can enable or disable Microphone, Calendar, or Notification permissions at any time via your device's app settings.
​Data Deletion: Clearing your app storage/cache will instantly delete all local browsing history, saved tasks, and offline data.
​Account & Sync Settings: If you link local calendar or task tools, you can disconnect them anytime through the app settings.
​7. Children's Privacy
​Wakanda Browser is not directed toward children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such data, please contact us to have it removed immediately.
​8. Updates to This Policy
​We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in functionality or legal requirements. Updated policies will be posted within the app along with a revised "Last Updated" date.
